ffmpeg
------

ffmpeg is invoked as an external process and never linked into Offstream. Nothing in this
repository is a derivative work of it, and its licence governs ffmpeg alone.

Releases bundle an unmodified LGPL-3.0-or-later build of ffmpeg, in the `ffmpeg` folder
beside the executable, along with its own LICENSE.txt and a SOURCE.txt naming the exact
commit it was built from. No GPL build is ever bundled: a GPL build would reach Offstream's
own licensing, and buys nothing this app uses - libmp3lame, libopus and native flac and aac
are all present in an LGPL build. A copy on the user's PATH, or one they point the setting
at, is used in preference and may be any build they like.

The precise build, its digest and its source are pinned in build/windows/ffmpeg.json.
Distributing an LGPL binary obliges distributing the source it was built from, and every
Offstream release attaches that source archive rather than offering to supply it later - an
offer has to outlive whatever was going to host it, and this one does not have to.

The bundled ffmpeg is never re-signed or otherwise altered on its way into a release. It
ships exactly as its publisher built it.


VB-CABLE
--------

VB-CABLE is not bundled. It is donationware from VB-Audio Software, installed by the user
from vb-audio.com; Offstream only detects whether it is present.
